---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description="Twelve weeks of workshop, lab and field time. Each studio carries one field objective, and your team books its own slot to fly it."
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Four hours of workshop and lab, and a field slot your team books itself.
    Every studio names the objective you are flying that week, who owns it, the
    number you are to predict before you measure it, what you do instead if the
    weather says no, and the one safety rule that matters most that day.
  </p>
  <p>
    The studios are not twelve versions of the same afternoon. Week 4 measures a
    glide, week 7 breaks a spar on a rig, week 10 switches your transmitter off
    on purpose. Read any two and you should be able to tell them apart.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
